<h2>A verified company and bid pack</h2><p>Subject to relevance, availability and the solicitation rules, a response may include a company profile, current legal or registration documents, contact details, verified team information with appropriate permission, relevant product or capability descriptions, technical approach, delivery plan, assumptions, exclusions and a commercial offer.</p><p>Fida will not add an unverified client, qualification, certificate, turnover, employee count, reference, result or partnership simply to complete a checklist. If a requested item is unavailable or does not apply, the response should state that clearly instead of replacing evidence with a claim.</p>
<h2>Requirements traceability and the technical offer</h2><p>A requirements matrix can connect each clause to the proposed response, evidence, configuration, development, integration, responsibility, dependency or deviation. This makes evaluation and later acceptance more accountable than a broad promise that the system “supports everything.”</p><ul><li>Functional workflows, reports and user roles</li><li>Non-functional requirements such as availability, performance and accessibility</li><li>Languages, locations, entities, currencies and deployment constraints</li><li>Data migration, integrations and external-provider dependencies</li><li>Security, privacy, audit, backup and recovery requirements</li><li>Training, documentation, support and service boundaries</li></ul>
<h2>Demonstrations, clarification and evaluation</h2><p>Where the procurement permits it, Fida can prepare a structured demonstration around representative scenarios. A demonstration should distinguish capabilities that already exist, items that require configuration, proposed development and external dependencies. Clarification answers and material changes should be recorded through the buyer’s authorized channel.</p><p>Evaluation criteria belong to the buyer. Fida can provide evidence and explanation, but cannot promise a score, award or procurement outcome.</p>
<h2>Contract and delivery readiness</h2><p>Before signature, both sides should understand the included scope, deliverables, milestones, acceptance criteria, client inputs, environments, data ownership, intellectual-property or licence terms, migration, integrations, security responsibilities, training, warranty or defect correction, support, hosting, payments and change control.</p><p>A realistic schedule must identify decisions, access, data, approvals and people required from the client as well as Fida’s delivery work. Dates and service levels are confirmed only in the signed agreement; this page is not a contractual commitment.</p>
<h2>Confidentiality, integrity and written communication</h2><p>Procurement documents and submissions may contain commercial, technical or personal information. The authorized parties should agree how documents are received, stored, shared and returned. Sensitive credentials and unrestricted production data should not be sent with an initial tender invitation.</p><p>Fida’s response should follow the applicable conflict, anti-fraud, confidentiality and communication requirements stated by the buyer. Any clarification, addendum or negotiation must use the authorized process.</p>
<h2>What to include with an invitation</h2><ul><li>Issuing organization and authorized procurement contact</li><li>Solicitation title, reference number and submission deadline</li><li>Complete instructions, scope or terms of reference</li><li>Evaluation method and mandatory eligibility documents</li><li>Submission format, language, channel and clarification deadline</li><li>Required validity, guarantee, contract and payment conditions</li><li>Security classification and rules for demonstrations or sample data</li></ul><p>Send documents through an authorized channel and identify confidential attachments. Fida can then confirm whether it can participate and which clarifications are required.</p>
<h2>Request a company profile</h2><p>If your organization is preparing market research, a supplier list or an upcoming procurement, request Fida’s current company profile and state which supporting documents you need. Availability is confirmed at the time of the request, and sensitive documents are shared only after the recipient and purpose are verified.</p>
